WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.870
George Caleb Bingham, a Missouri painter,

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.840
made this famous scene
of Daniel Boone leading settlers

3
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.050
through the Cumberland Gap into Kentucky.

4
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.990
Look at how it's built.

5
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:13.480
Boone strides toward you with his rifle.
His wife, Rebecca,

6
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.210
rides a white horse at the center,
almost like a holy figure.

7
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.750
The settlers emerge from a dark,
broken wilderness.

8
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:27.130
Danger is suggested, rifles ready,
but no Native people and no fighting appear.

9
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:32.550
The Cherokee and Shawnee, who fought hard
to keep Kentucky, are simply missing.
